            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0412" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.E/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-05T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1923—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>20. Your confidential telegram Number 16, March 1, 1 P.M. The following <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide memoire</hi> was given the Brazilian Ambassador
                    to-day:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> quoted in
                    telegram no. 23, March 5, to Ambassador in Brazil, printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>The foregoing is for your confidential information only and you need take no
                    action thereon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
